content.study:
Section 5 is the gateway provision. A marriage may be solemnised between any two Hindus if:
(i) neither has a spouse living;
(ii) neither is incapable of valid consent by unsoundness of mind, or suffers mental disorder making them unfit for marriage and procreation, or has recurrent attacks of insanity;
(iii) bridegroom has completed 21 years and bride 18 years;
(iv) parties are not within degrees of prohibited relationship, unless custom governing each permits;
(v) parties are not sapindas of each other, unless custom governing each permits.

Ceremony is governed by s. 7. Registration under s. 8 is facilitative.

Consequences: breach of (i)/(iv)/(v) → void under s. 11; certain mental conditions, force, fraud, pregnancy by another → voidable under s. 12; bigamy also attracts s. 17; other contraventions may attract s. 18. Custom exception applies only to (iv) and (v), not to monogamy.

Case-law verification remains a separate gate.
